s writing and prioritization frameworks"}], "description": "Students learn to treat conversion improvement as a disciplined process of diagnosis, hypothesis, testing, and iteration."}]}, {"id": "51f9dd89-4f62-45b0-9edf-e2523817b0e7", "type": "topic", "title": "Search Engine Optimization and Organic Discoverability", "description": "Build search visibility through intent research, technical SEO, content quality, authority, and measurement.", "children": [{"id": "c66a3641-fc1a-4361-9244-29dd73bc752a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Search intent and keyword strategy", "children": [{"id": "19b3c18a-294b-4df0-8812-bf94b871002c", "type": "concept", "title": "Informational, commercial, navigational, and transactional intent"}, {"id": "11efdf9c-42b4-4e58-9221-8909326911d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Keyword clusters and topic maps"}, {"id": "29b0037b-62d9-4bfb-a6f4-ff510309bd7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Search volume, difficulty, and business value"}, {"id": "bc76583b-3818-4b94-a1b5-18d8d309ac92", "type": "concept", "title": "SERP features and zero-click behavior"}], "description": "SEO begins with understanding what people are trying to accomplish when they search. Students learn to map queries to intent and content formats."}, {"id": "d13e4e3c-d1df-4f82-ac2c-5237123d14f5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "On-page and content SEO", "children": [{"id": "26afedaa-cb81-4762-917f-8dc058027083", "type": "concept", "title": "Titles, headings, metadata, and internal linking"}, {"id": "72c038ab-0c34-46f8-a7b4-b35a5e24ba63", "type": "concept", "title": "E-E-A-T and content quality signals"}, {"id": "a9c6ef40-7b96-4feb-aaeb-ebdd35b5766c", "type": "concept", "title": "Content refreshes and pruning"}, {"id": "84cb7fe2-6de1-4fd1-9abf-44b081f8a9c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Image, video, and structured content optimization"}], "description": "This subtopic covers how useful, trustworthy content becomes discoverable and persuasive."}, {"id": "de5bf2cd-7ff0-4a8c-999d-12106d0f8546